{"parentUuid":"42b9e900-c217-450d-868b-f66b25a447e9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SSrHDAqb9dk4cUWTrProto","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Pumpkin solver TU Delft Rust LCG 0.3.0 GitHub 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin: A Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin\"},{\"title\":\"pumpkin_solver - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver/latest/pumpkin_solver/\"},{\"title\":\"ConSoL Lab · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ConSol-Lab\"},{\"title\":\"Unite and Lead: Finding Disjunctive Cliques for Scheduling Problems\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.35\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin/issues\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ztlpn/minilp: A pure Rust linear programming solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ztlpn/minilp\"},{\"title\":\"Goals - Rust Project Goals\",\"url\":\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/2026/goals.html\"},{\"title\":\"👋 Introduction - Rust Project Goals\",\"url\":\"https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-project-goals/\"},{\"title\":\"awesome-rust/README.md at master · uhub/awesome-rust\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/uhub/awesome-rust/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Pumpkin MC · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Pumpkin-MC\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Pumpkin:\n\nPumpkin is a combinatorial optimisation solver developed by the ConSol Lab at TU Delft. It is based on the (lazy clause generation) constraint programming paradigm. Since Pumpkin is written in pure Rust, it is easy to install!\n\nThe solver was developed using the lazy clause generation (LCG) constraint programming approach, and has recent academic work published in the Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence in March 2026.\n\nThe project is available on GitHub at https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin. However, the search results did not contain specific information about version 0.3.0 or details about that particular release.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8032d766-7005-4ce3-a2d0-30fe0f1ac37c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:22.529Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"42b9e900-c217-450d-868b-f66b25a447e9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c8a116bf-1e65-45ba-a8bf-23a636671cdc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ttCrhX9w1WvZ7UwbFQ8Ri","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Glasgow Constraint Solver ciaranm VeriPB cumulative alldifferent CP 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver: A constraint programming solver with support for proof logging · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-subgraph-solver: A solver for subgraph isomorphism problems, based upon a series of papers by subsets of McCreesh, Prosser, and Trimble. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-subgraph-solver\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-51372-6_19\"},{\"title\":\"CP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cp2025.a4cp.org/\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7314700/\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming, CP 2025, Glasgow, Scotland, August 10-15, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/cp/2025.html\"},{\"title\":\"Ciaran McCreesh\",\"url\":\"https://ciaranm.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver/releases\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/The-Glasgow-Subgraph-Solver:-Using-Constraint-to-McCreesh-Prosser/d25dccef7e17f0af733509377f577390f0933a3b\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard\",\"url\":\"https://ciaranm.github.io/papers/icgt2020-glasgow-subgraph-solver.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found related to your query:\n\n## Glasgow Constraint Solver\n\nThe Glasgow Constraint Solver is a constraint programming solver with a key feature of the ability to produce proof logs, currently using the VeriPB 3.0 format. The solver can run the VeriPB proof checker on the \"find all solutions\" search tree, to check that the OPB definition is consistent.\n\n## VeriPB Integration\n\nIf the instance is satisfiable, the solver gives a witness in pseudo-Boolean form, and if unsatisfiable, provides a proof in VeriPB format that the pseudo-Boolean instance is unsatisfiable.\n\n## Related Constraint Programming Work\n\nThe GitHub repository for the Glasgow Constraint Solver is maintained by ciaranm (Ciaran McCreesh) and contains various constraint types in the gcs/constraints/ directory.\n\n## CP 2025 Conference\n\nCP 2025, the International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming, is scheduled for August 10-15, 2025, in Glasgow, Scotland.\n\nThe search results show active development on constraint programming solvers with proof logging capabilities, though specific details about cumulative and alldifferent constraints in this context are not extensively detailed in the available search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"40d07c23-f0de-4775-85a3-e96845c656ee","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:25.037Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c8a116bf-1e65-45ba-a8bf-23a636671cdc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2bf83aca-b53e-4b85-b522-846150e32f28","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016fWStvbLUwe6nersstm9Gu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Pumpkin Rust constraint solver SAT competition 2025 DRAT proof certificate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin: A Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin\"},{\"title\":\"pumpkin_solver - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver\"},{\"title\":\"RustSAT: A Library for SAT Solving in Rust - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.15\"},{\"title\":\"Varisat Manual\",\"url\":\"https://jix.github.io/varisat/manual/0.2.1/print.html\"},{\"title\":\"sat-solver · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/sat-solver?l=rust\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - xgillard/rsolve: A sat solver in rust · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/xgillard/rsolve\"},{\"title\":\"splr - crates.io: Rust Package Registry\",\"url\":\"https://crates.io/crates/splr\"},{\"title\":\"Expressing Symmetry Breaking in DRAT Proofs\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~mheule/publications/sbp.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Proof Traces for SAT solvers | Wonderings of a SAT geek\",\"url\":\"https://www.msoos.org/2022/04/proof-traces-for-sat-solvers/\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Pumpkin, the Rust constraint solver, and related information:\n\n## Pumpkin Solver\n\nPumpkin is a Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. It is a combinatorial optimisation solver developed by the ConSol Lab at TU Delft and is based on the lazy clause generation constraint programming paradigm.\n\n## Proof Certificates and DRAT Support\n\nPumpkin supports proof logging for SAT and CP problems, and during search, the solver produces a ProofLog, which is a list of deductions made by the solver. A unique feature of Pumpkin is that it can produce a certificate of unsatisfiability.\n\n## DRAT Format in SAT Competitions\n\nDRAT is the de-facto standard format for unsatisfiability proofs and is required for solvers taking part in the yearly SAT competition. It is a minimal clausal proof format that lists additions and removals of clauses, does not contain any justification for clause additions, and makes DRAT proofs easy and efficient to generate and comparatively compact, but involves more work during checking.\n\nThe search results confirm that Pumpkin is an active constraint solving project with certification capabilities, though specific details about Pumpkin's participation in the 2025 SAT competition were not found in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8601a015-1bce-4022-a92e-04c761e729e7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:27.596Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2bf83aca-b53e-4b85-b522-846150e32f28","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
