{"parentUuid":"0cb9557d-016c-400b-bbe6-de540c710a8f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BnghTE1qVVSkzAdVbWXcqe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kqu8BEr4gCPgD4rTxotjjq","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver/latest/pumpkin_solver/","prompt":"Extract: API surface, supported constraints list, propagators list, Python binding mention, version number, FlatZinc support, examples"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3693,"cache_read_input_tokens":21287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3693,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotdZSGwUZzy33si3NUK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"16693d9f-fbff-48d2-a15e-8568ac6ea6e2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:35.626Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"024d48f5-19cb-4548-8063-b0080f8c831a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EbgP2avAwH7yH73d9is3Ke","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pumpkin Constraint Programming Solver\n\n**Latest Release:** v0.3.0 (February 11, 2026)\n\n**Licenses:** Apache-2.0 and MIT\n\n## Supported Global Constraints\n\nPumpkin implements:\n- Cumulative and disjunctive scheduling constraints\n- Element constraint\n- Arithmetic operations (linear inequalities, division, multiplication, maximum, absolute value)\n- Clausal constraints\n\nNote: The repository does not list all_different, no_overlap, circuit, or table constraints in its current capabilities.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Python Bindings:** Available via `pumpkin-solver-py`\n- **FlatZinc Support:** Yes, for constraint modeling\n- **MiniZinc Integration:** Serves as a backend solver; won bronze medal in the 2025 MiniZinc Challenge fixed search track\n- **Proof Logging:** Unique capability to produce certificates of unsatisfiability\n\n## Development Status\n\nActive development with 594 commits on main branch. The project emphasizes \"easy-to-use, and well-documented\" implementation in pure Rust with strong contribution guidelines requiring thorough documentation."}]},"uuid":"3f51519f-987d-49ee-a253-f9a94f34339d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:38.145Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"024d48f5-19cb-4548-8063-b0080f8c831a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0cb9557d-016c-400b-bbe6-de540c710a8f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EuDzeLQVsXfd9obmFVP9mj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Glasgow Constraint Solver - Key Information\n\n**Latest Commit:** The repository shows 1,211 commits on the main branch, but the specific latest commit date is not displayed in the provided content.\n\n**Build System & Language:** Written in C++ (93.9% of codebase) with CMake 3.21+ required. \"A C++23 compiler. GCC 13 (Ubuntu 24.04) is the oldest tested; GCC 15 and Clang 21 are the primary development compilers.\"\n\n**Supported Constraints:** The documentation mentions NotEquals, Table (extensional constraints), and WeightedSum (linear inequalities). The code includes a `gcs/constraints/` directory, though the full constraint list isn't enumerated in the visible content. Notably, cumulative and element constraints aren't explicitly mentioned in the provided excerpt.\n\n**Python Binding:** A `python/` directory exists in the repository structure, indicating Python support is available.\n\n**Modeling Languages:** \n- MiniZinc/FlatZinc support via the `minizinc/` directory\n- XCSP support via `xcsp/` directory (optional, can be disabled)\n\n**Proof Logging:** Uses \"VeriPB 3.0 format\" for proof verification. The solver outputs `.opb` (low-level model) and `.pbp` (proof) files verifiable with the VeriPB checker.\n\n**License:** MIT license\n\n**Examples:** Includes cake, crystal maze, sudoku, and magic square example programs in the `examples/` directory.\n\n**Benchmarks:** Contains `minicp_benchmarks/` directory for performance testing."}]},"uuid":"c290e3a1-a059-46eb-ab40-1c7d0f4aab2f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:41.199Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cb9557d-016c-400b-bbe6-de540c710a8f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"16693d9f-fbff-48d2-a15e-8568ac6ea6e2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kqu8BEr4gCPgD4rTxotjjq","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pumpkin Solver: API Surface & Features\n\n## Version & Licensing\n**Version 0.3.0** is available under \"MIT OR Apache-2.0\" dual licensing.\n\n## Core API Surface\nThe main interaction point is the `Solver` struct, which enables variable creation, constraint addition, and problem solving. Key methods include:\n- `satisfy()` - find a solution\n- `optimise()` - find optimal solutions\n- `get_solution_iterator()` - obtain multiple solutions\n- `satisfy_under_assumptions()` - solve with assumptions for unsatisfiable core extraction\n\n## Supported Constraints\n\n**Global constraints:**\n- Cumulative\n- Element\n- All-different\n- Disjunctive (NoOverlap)\n- Table (positive/negative)\n\n**Arithmetic constraints:**\n- Linear integer (in)equalities\n- Integer division, multiplication\n- Maximum, minimum, absolute value\n- Clausal constraints\n\n**Additional types:**\n- Boolean weighted constraints\n- Conjunction/disjunction\n\n## Notable Features\n- **FlatZinc support** via the `flatzinc` dependency (0.3.21)\n- **Unsatisfiability certificates** - produces \"certificate of unsatisfiability\" per CP'24 research\n- **Pure Rust implementation** following best practices\n- **No Python bindings mentioned** in this documentation\n\n## Build Dependencies\nIncludes `cc ^1.1.30`, suggesting C/C++ interop capability (likely for constraint solver components)."}]},"uuid":"c39c1d23-8120-4268-b2b2-7087588a9940","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:07:42.606Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16693d9f-fbff-48d2-a15e-8568ac6ea6e2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
