{"parentUuid":"75dbc52b-07db-497e-aa00-1cf96b502fcf","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M9fac1dgRdcHu3HgcvmCn4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NKMcLwTuf3cgR9TiiWdVUw","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"Glasgow Constraint Solver\" cumulative paper \"proof logging\" 2025 2026 McCreesh"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2023,"cache_read_input_tokens":30580,"output_tokens":336,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2023},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":30580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2023,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotgPXJcX9dRAdr4v4Es","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3bdd315a-714a-4e6e-8b35-855cfb4364c0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:11.284Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"75dbc52b-07db-497e-aa00-1cf96b502fcf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kwyp4gG1BZpbhqXnWgWye6","type":"tool_result","content":"# Glasgow Constraint Solver - Releases Overview\n\nThe repository contains four academic releases:\n\n1. **AAAI2025** (December 16, 2024) - Most recent\n   - Associated with \"Certifying Bounds Propagation for Integer Multiplication Constraints\"\n   - Presented at The 39th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n\n2. **CPAIOR2024** (March 21, 2024)\n   - Related to \"Proof Logging for the Circuit Constraint\"\n   - From The 21st International Conference on Constraint Programming, AI, and Operations Research\n\n3. **CP2023** (July 10, 2023)\n   - Covers \"Proof Logging for Smart Extensional Constraints\"\n   - Associated with The 29th International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming\n\n4. **CP2022** (May 3, 2022)\n   - Connected to \"An Auditable Constraint Programming Solver\"\n   - From The 28th International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming\n\nEach release represents a milestone tied to peer-reviewed academic publications in constraint programming and artificial intelligence. The project maintains steady activity with releases approximately annually since 2022."}]},"uuid":"327f6161-c4ac-4b2c-8f9b-2ac75f0c4846","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:15.070Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"75dbc52b-07db-497e-aa00-1cf96b502fcf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9c543e41-8564-49a2-b926-596782a50939","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013eVB2BFiKJhewxKkoysjM7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pumpkin Repository Releases\n\nBased on the GitHub releases page, here are the documented releases in reverse chronological order:\n\n## Recent Releases\n\n**pumpkin-solver-v0.3.0** (11 Feb)\n- Fixed binary equality issue in logging\n- Updated Rust edition to 2024\n- Integrated proof checker into tests\n\n**fzn-rs-v0.1.0** (10 Feb)\n- Introduced a new FlatZinc parser designed for easier reuse\n\n**pumpkin-solver: v0.2.2** (10 Nov)\n- Added brancher statistics logging\n- Implemented support for unbounded integers in FlatZinc\n- Enhanced disjunctive constraint handling with edge-finding\n\n**pumpkin-core: v0.2.2** (10 Nov)\n- Multiple constraint improvements and performance optimizations\n- Added lazy explanation support for linear constraints\n- Implemented gzip encoding for proofs\n\n**pumpkin-solver: v0.2.1** (10 Jul)\n- Added table and negative table constraint implementations\n- Improved FlatZinc search strategy handling\n- Various bug fixes for proof logging\n\n**pumpkin-solver: v0.2.0** (11 Apr)\n- Introduced lower-bounding search functionality\n- Added brancher logging capabilities\n- Implemented lazy explanation context\n\nThe most recent activity shows commits from February of the current year, with v0.3.0 being the latest documented release."}]},"uuid":"751fb061-b184-4d0e-bfec-13a92d19d229","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:15.423Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c543e41-8564-49a2-b926-596782a50939","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3bdd315a-714a-4e6e-8b35-855cfb4364c0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKMcLwTuf3cgR9TiiWdVUw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Glasgow Constraint Solver\" cumulative paper \"proof logging\" 2025 2026 McCreesh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Ciaran McCreesh\",\"url\":\"https://ciaranm.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver: A constraint programming solver with support for proof logging · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-subgraph-solver: A solver for subgraph isomorphism problems, based upon a series of papers by subsets of McCreesh, Prosser, and Trimble. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-subgraph-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Ciaran McCreesh's research works | University of Glasgow and other places\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Ciaran-McCreesh-84949949\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver Ciaran McCreesh Patrick Prosser James Trimble\",\"url\":\"https://www.dcs.gla.ac.uk/~ciaran/talks/2020-06-icgt-gss.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/The-Glasgow-Subgraph-Solver:-Using-Constraint-to-McCreesh-Prosser/d25dccef7e17f0af733509377f577390f0933a3b\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-51372-6_19\"},{\"title\":\"The Glasgow Subgraph Solver: Using Constraint Programming to Tackle Hard Subgraph Isomorphism Problem Variants | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/342441551_The_Glasgow_Subgraph_Solver_Using_Constraint_Programming_to_Tackle_Hard_Subgraph_Isomorphism_Problem_Variants\"},{\"title\":\"Proof Logging for Smart Extensional Constraints - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2023.26\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding the Glasgow Constraint Solver, cumulative constraints, proof logging, and recent work by McCreesh:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Glasgow Constraint Solver is a new project that brings proof logging to constraint programming.\n\n## Recent Publications (2025-2026)\n\nThe search results reveal several recent papers from this research line:\n\n1. **AAAI 2026**: Markus Anders, Bart Bogaerts, Benjamin Bogø, Arthur Gontier, Wietze Koops, Ciaran McCreesh, and others published \"Faster Certified Symmetry Breaking using Orders with Auxiliary Variables\" at AAAI 2026.\n\n2. **AAAI 2025**: Matthew J. McIlree and Ciaran McCreesh published \"Certifying Bounds Propagation for Integer Multiplication Constraints\" at AAAI 2025.\n\n## Proof Logging Focus\n\nA constraint programming solver that implements proof logging will output a machine-checkable certificate of correctness alongside any result it obtains, providing an auditable way of guaranteeing that a solver has produced a correct answer using sound reasoning.\n\nThe search results indicate active development of the Glasgow Constraint Solver with proof logging support, though I did not find specific papers focusing specifically on cumulative constraints in the 2025-2026 timeframe in these results. If you need more specific information about cumulative constraint papers, you may want to check McCreesh's personal research page or the GitHub repository directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cb41aaf8-ed07-4b5a-a8e1-f50a3e6ff714","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:21.099Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3bdd315a-714a-4e6e-8b35-855cfb4364c0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
