{"parentUuid":"a9a04f99-870e-4a15-968d-b7ec32904e6c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FK1GvqAhVy1NHK8eXJNpGK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XcZiyhSgZDw6o1NgWodMBq","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Pumpkin solver Benders decomposition routing flow CP-SAT alternative"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2822,"cache_read_input_tokens":32603,"output_tokens":328,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2822},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":328,"cache_read_input_tokens":32603,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2822,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaothXdVDUfCstdZPRf5H","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"28f5a0a1-10be-4aa7-919e-e00381564141","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:26.339Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"36360320-00ab-482c-8796-39cc4e2d5dfe","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MyU4bLKWhAkEAbPEr679pW","type":"tool_result","content":"# Recent Papers 2024-2026: Constraint Solving & Proof Logging\n\nBased on the webpage, here are the relevant recent publications:\n\n## 2026\n**Faster Certified Symmetry Breaking using Orders with Auxiliary Variables** (AAAI 2026)\n- Authors: Markus Anders, Bart Bogaerts, Benjamin Bogø, Arthur Gontier, Wietze Koops, Ciaran McCreesh, Magnus O. Myreen, Jakob Nordström, Andy Oertel, Adrian Rebola-Pardo, Yong Kiam Tan\n- Focuses on symmetry breaking techniques with certified solutions\n\n## 2025\n**Certifying Bounds Propagation for Integer Multiplication Constraints** (AAAI 2025)\n- Authors: Matthew J. McIlree and Ciaran McCreesh\n- Addresses proof logging for arithmetic constraints in constraint programming\n\n## 2024\n**Pseudo-Boolean Reasoning About States and Transitions to Certify Dynamic Programming and Decision Diagram Algorithms** (CP 2024)\n- Authors: Emir Demirović, Ciaran McCreesh, Matthew J. McIlree, Jakob Nordström, Andy Oertel, Konstantin Sidorov\n- Extends certification approaches to dynamic programming\n\n**Proof Logging for the Circuit Constraint** (CPAIOR 2024)\n- Authors: Matthew J. McIlree, Ciaran McCreesh, Jakob Nordström\n- Develops proof logging specifically for circuit constraints\n\n**End-to-End Verification for Subgraph Solving** (AAAI 2024)\n- Authors: Stephan Gocht, Ciaran McCreesh, Magnus O. Myreen, Jakob Nordström, Andy Oertel, Yong Kiam Tan\n\n---\n\n**Note:** The webpage does not list papers specifically addressing cumulative, alldifferent, scheduling, or large benchmarks in 2024-2026. The Glasgow Constraint Solver project is mentioned as \"a new project that brings proof logging to constraint programming,\" but detailed papers on that solver appear to focus on proof certification rather than specific constraint types."}]},"uuid":"6b69fc7b-0268-4ee8-b8e9-97f48c000b28","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:33.098Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"36360320-00ab-482c-8796-39cc4e2d5dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a9a04f99-870e-4a15-968d-b7ec32904e6c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016QVWDRbQ4rW8u8HBd3MoAk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy Python constraint programming library Pumpkin Glasgow OR-Tools backend comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - CPMpy/cpmpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling library in Python, based on numpy, with direct solver access. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpmpy/\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy 0.9.28 on PyPI - Libraries.io - security & maintenance data for open source software\",\"url\":\"https://libraries.io/pypi/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/pumpkin/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling in Python — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/min_max_bug/\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling in Python — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Modeling and solving with CPMpy — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/modeling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy cpo interface (cpmpy.solvers.cpo) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/pumpkin/api/solvers/cpo.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.gcs — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/pumpkin/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/gcs.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - CPMpy/PyConA: A cpmpy-based library for constraint acquisition. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/pycona\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's an overview of CPMpy and the backend solvers you asked about:\n\n## CPMpy Overview\n\nCPMpy is a Constraint Programming and Modeling library in Python, based on numpy, with direct solver access. CPMpy is part of the scientific Python ecosystem, making it easy to use in Jupyter notebooks, to add visualisations, or to use it in machine learning pipelines.\n\n## Supported Backends\n\nCPMpy supports CP Solvers including OR-Tools (default), IBM CP Optimizer (license required), Choco, Glasgow GCS, Pumpkin, and MiniZinc+solvers.\n\n### Specific Backend Information:\n\n**OR-Tools:** The OR-Tools CP-SAT solver is an award-winning constraint programming solver that uses SAT (satisfiability) methods and lazy-clause generation. The 'ortools' python package is bundled by default with CPMpy.\n\n**Glasgow Constraint Solver (GCS):** The key feature of this CP solver is the ability to produce proof logs.\n\n**Pumpkin and other solvers:** While Pumpkin is listed as one of the supported backends, the search results don't provide specific comparative details about these individual solvers.\n\n## Performance Guidance\n\nCPMpy's rule-of-thumb ordering when solving a problem is: OrTools > Gurobi > Exact > Others. However, Different solvers excell at different problems.\n\nFor more detailed comparisons between these specific backends, you may want to consult CPMpy's documentation or research papers on constraint programming solver performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"09cead92-3270-4bd9-94c7-29ffb2a6891c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:33.109Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a9a04f99-870e-4a15-968d-b7ec32904e6c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"28f5a0a1-10be-4aa7-919e-e00381564141","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcZiyhSgZDw6o1NgWodMBq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Pumpkin solver Benders decomposition routing flow CP-SAT alternative\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Model-based Decomposition Algorithms for Complex Routing ...\",\"url\":\"https://tidel.mie.utoronto.ca/pubs/Theses/Zhang_Jiachen_202510_PhD_thesis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A logic-based Benders decomposition for microscopic railway timetable planning - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221722001643\"},{\"title\":\"An enhanced Benders decomposition method for unique shortest path routing | OPSEARCH | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12597-023-00718-0\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - JuMP-dev\",\"url\":\"https://jump.dev/JuMP.jl/stable/tutorials/algorithms/benders_decomposition/\"},{\"title\":\"The Benders Decomposition Algorithm: A Literature Review Ragheb Rahmaniani\",\"url\":\"https://www.cirrelt.ca/documentstravail/cirrelt-2016-30.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"An effective benders decomposition algorithm for solving the distributed permutation flowshop scheduling problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054820301234\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing Automatic Benders Decomposition in a Modern MIP Solver | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/340629033_Implementing_Automatic_Benders_Decomposition_in_a_Modern_MIP_Solver\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about Benders decomposition, routing, flow problems, and CP-SAT. Here's a summary of the key findings:\n\n## Overview of Relevant Technologies\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver, making it a competitive option for optimization problems.\n\n## Benders Decomposition for Routing and Flow Problems\n\nBenders decomposition decomposes a problem into one integer-programming master problem containing routing decision variables and one linear-programming subproblem that copes with path length constraints. Enhanced Benders decomposition methods can be embedded with redundancy generation strategy based on the study of problem properties of network flow problems.\n\n## Constraint Programming and Logic-Based Approaches\n\nConstraint Programming (CP) can be a better choice than mixed integer programming (MIP) solvers because of its greater ability to handle special constraints, and improvements of several orders of magnitude have been observed when the master problem was solved by CP rather than MIP for scheduling and routing problems.\n\nLogic-Based Benders Decomposition (LBBD) is a generalization of classical Benders decomposition that integrates combinatorial, constraint-oriented subproblems and employs logic-based inference to generate exclusion and optimality cuts, facilitating rapid convergence even in NP-hard, nonconvex scenarios.\n\n## Integration with Modern Solvers\n\nModern implementations of Benders decomposition rely on a single search tree, where Benders subproblems are solved at every integer-solution node in the Branch-and-Cut tree through cut callback functionality, a variant often called Branch-and-Benders-Cut, which IBM ILOG CPLEX implements as automatic Benders decomposition.\n\nThe search results do not contain specific information about a \"Pumpkin solver\" in relation to these techniques, so I cannot comment on that particular tool.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8a79f2a7-ee12-4140-a8a6-2e96b72c0e28","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:34.946Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28f5a0a1-10be-4aa7-919e-e00381564141","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
