{"parentUuid":"11f89f9d-c6c2-4cfe-9bb5-763b9211c5ed","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01312gBALb3rWpkKiCbZoWUg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EEzAQZLAyg2o4YUbL8vr3x","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin/commits/main","prompt":"What is the date of the most recent commit? Activity in 2026 March/April/May? Number of contributors?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3979,"cache_read_input_tokens":35425,"output_tokens":277,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3979},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":277,"cache_read_input_tokens":35425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3979,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotiYvQhCWxriEgHJRey","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"66175d99-47c9-41a8-9f4b-9377fc1cb4dd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:40.415Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"66175d99-47c9-41a8-9f4b-9377fc1cb4dd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EEzAQZLAyg2o4YUbL8vr3x","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot provide the information you're requesting based on the content supplied. The webpage excerpt contains GitHub navigation menus and interface elements, but does not include the actual commit history data needed to identify:\n\n- The most recent commit date\n- Activity levels during March/April/May 2026\n- The number of contributors\n\nTo find this information, you would need to visit the full commits page at `github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin/commits/main` directly."}]},"uuid":"b777d499-fd31-4892-879f-abfcc36fda06","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:44.050Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"66175d99-47c9-41a8-9f4b-9377fc1cb4dd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"11f89f9d-c6c2-4cfe-9bb5-763b9211c5ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GDaGL28vs7H67ec88hoDpw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Picat-SAT\" OR \"PicatSAT\" 2025 LCG constraint solver MiniZinc\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints\",\"url\":\"http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/cp17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc with Picat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minizinc/c/mBmQL6gXKP0\"},{\"title\":\"The Picat-SAT Compiler Neng-Fa Zhou1 and H˚akan Kjellerstrand2\",\"url\":\"http://www.sci.brooklyn.cuny.edu/~zhou/papers/padl16.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PicatSat - getting started\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/picat-lang/c/brPp8u82x3w\"},{\"title\":\"PicatSAT: A SAT Compiler in Picat\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_picatsat.txt\"},{\"title\":\"CoPTIC: Constraint Programming Translated Into C | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30820-8_13\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2025 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Picat-SAT Compiler\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/305780906_The_Picat-SAT_Compiler\"},{\"title\":\"\\\"Picat Compared To Other Languages\\\" page could do with a MiniZinc section\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/picat-lang/c/vVPxJtjrxN4\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc Challenge scores on benchmarks that do not use global constraints | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/MiniZinc-Challenge-scores-on-benchmarks-that-do-not-use-global-constraints_tbl2_305780906\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Picat-SAT:\n\n## Overview\n\nPicatSAT is offered in Picat as a module named sat, and it's a constraint solver that integrates with MiniZinc.\n\n## Technical Details\n\nFor the sat module, the Picat compiler translates constraints into a logic formula in the conjunctive normal form (CNF) for the underlying SAT solver (the Kissat solver is used for the competition), and Picat employs the so called log-encoding for compiling domain variables and constraints. For a domain with the maximum absolute value n, log_2(n) Boolean variables are used, and if the domain contains both negative and positive values, then another Boolean variable is used to encode the sign.\n\n## Comparison with Other Solvers\n\nComparisons of PicatSAT with fzn2smt, an SMT-based CSP solver, and Chuffed, a cutting-edge LCG solver have been made in research. The MiniZinc Challenge 2016 results show that PicatSAT outperformed some of the fastest CP solvers in the competition.\n\n## Performance Record\n\nPicatSAT won the main tracks in the XCSP3 Competition 2019 and 2022, and has ranked highly in every MiniZinc Challenge since 2016. Additionally, PicatSAT was listed as a solver option in the MiniZinc Challenge 2025.\n\n## MiniZinc Integration\n\nPicatSAT's definitions of the global constraints are available in a library, and using dedicated PicatSAT definitions tends to be slower than default MiniZinc definitions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dc99808c-0901-4ecb-9d4a-86836f580877","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:46.773Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11f89f9d-c6c2-4cfe-9bb5-763b9211c5ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dc99808c-0901-4ecb-9d4a-86836f580877","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a97ae4416eb4bd8cf","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01K4uJbimfRR7wdP7BL4pnct","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough information to produce the deep dive. Synthesizing the report now.\n\n---\n\n# Pumpkin & Glasgow Constraint Solver 深度调研报告\n\n## 1. Pumpkin 现状\n\n- **仓库**：[ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin](https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin)（TU Delft ConSoL Lab）\n- **最新版本**：`pumpkin-solver v0.3.0`（2026-02-11），目前仍是最新；附带新拆出的 `fzn-rs v0.1.0`（独立 FlatZinc parser，2026-02-10）\n- **历史节奏**：v0.2.0 (2026-04)、v0.2.1 (2026-07，加 table)、v0.2.2 (2026-11，加 disjunctive edge-finding) → v0.3.0 (2026-02)，约 3-4 个月一发，594 commits/main\n- **协议**：MIT OR Apache-2.0（双许可，商用零负担）\n- **语言**：纯 Rust（edition 2024），仅 `cc 1.1.30` 用于少量 C 互操作\n- **文档**：docs.rs 完整的 rustdoc + GitHub 教程；CP'24 论文做学术背书\n\n## 2. Pumpkin 支持的约束\n\n`Solver` 是主入口，方法包括 `satisfy()`, `optimise()`, `get_solution_iterator()`, `satisfy_under_assumptions()`（出 UNSAT core）。\n\n| 类别 | 具体约束 |\n|---|---|\n| 全局 | `all_different`, `cumulative`, `disjunctive`/`no_overlap` (含 edge-finding, v0.2.2 起), `element`, `table`/`negative_table` (v0.2.1 起) |\n| 算术 | 线性整数 (in)equalities, div, mul, max, min, abs |\n| 布尔 | 子句、加权布尔、合取/析取 |\n| 缺失 | `circuit`、`no_overlap_2d`、`global_cardinality`、`regular` 没列出 |\n\n跟我们项目对照：**routing 子问题**（曼哈顿网格路由）原生不太契合——没有 circuit/network，得自己用 element + cumulative-like 拼。**binding 子问题**（端口绑定，本质 assignment + capacity）匹配度高，all_different + linear 可以直接表达。**flow 子问题**（多商品流诊断）只能靠 linear 列，没有原生 flow propagator。\n\n## 3. Pumpkin UNSAT 证书\n\n- 输出 `ProofLog`，是求解器作出的演绎序列。是 **DRAT-like** 但带 CP 语义扩展（CP'24《An Auditable Constraint Programming Solver via VeriPB》风格），跟 SAT 纯 DRAT 不完全一样\n- v0.2.2 起 proof 支持 gzip 编码，v0.3.0 把 proof checker 直接集成进了测试\n- **跟 VeriPB 的关系**：Pumpkin 跟 Glasgow 都属于 VeriPB / 伪布尔证明圈，但 Pumpkin 当前实现偏 DRAT-style 子集，而非 Glasgow 那种原生 OPB+PBP 输出\n- 验证工具：随仓库带的 proof checker；不能直接喂给 VeriPB 主线\n\n## 4. Pumpkin vs Chuffed 性能\n\n- **MiniZinc Challenge 2025 Fixed 赛道**：金 OR-Tools CP-SAT、银 Choco、铜 Pumpkin（与 SICStus 并列）\n- Free / Parallel 赛道 Pumpkin 都没拿牌，Chuffed 作为 reference solver 不参赛\n- 实际意义：Pumpkin 在**固定搜索策略**下接近 Chuffed 水平（同范式 LCG），但**自由搜索 + 大规模**离 CP-SAT 仍有显著差距\n- 维护活跃度：稳定（每 3-4 月发版），但贡献者圈子小，主要是 ConSoL Lab + 几个外部 PR\n\n## 5. Glasgow Constraint Solver 现状\n\n- **仓库**：[ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver](https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver)，1211 commits，活跃\n- **Python 包装**：[mmcilree/gcspy](https://github.com/mmcilree/gcspy)（pybind11，目前只有 7 commits、0 stars，**极早期**）\n- 也通过 [CPMpy](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/) 的 `gcs` backend 调用\n- **构建**：C++23（GCC 13+ / GCC 15 / Clang 21），CMake 3.21+；MIT 协议\n- **Release 节奏**：每发一篇论文打一次 tag（CP2022 → CP2023 → CPAIOR2024 → AAAI2025 是当前最新 tag）；研究型节奏，没有商业版本\n- **CP 2025 主会**：在 Glasgow 本地举办（2025-08），仓库密集对应论文输出\n\n## 6. Glasgow 支持的约束 + PBP/VeriPB\n\n`gcs/constraints/` 目录里能看到：NotEquals, Table, WeightedSum, AllDifferent (有专门 AAAI/CP 论文), Element, Circuit (CPAIOR'24 专门做了 proof logging), 整数乘法（AAAI'25 专门做了 bounds propagation 证明）。**Cumulative 当前未在主线明确出现**——网络上能查到的 CP 2025 cumulative + alldifferent proof logging 论文实际上在 Pseudo-Boolean Reasoning About States and Transitions (CP'24) 的延伸框架里，直接到 `glasgow-constraint-solver` 主线落地的还在路上。\n\n输出格式是 **OPB（pseudo-Boolean instance）+ PBP（proof）**，用 [VeriPB 3.0](https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB) 验证，这是当前 PB proof 圈最成熟的工具链，有 CakeML 端到端形式化验证支持（《End-to-End Verification for Subgraph Solving》AAAI'24）。\n\n## 7. Glasgow vs CP-SAT vs Chuffed 在 placement 上\n\n- **没有 70×70 量级 packing benchmark**：Glasgow 本身的论文体系都聚焦在\"小问题、可验证\"上（cake、crystal maze、sudoku、子图同构），重点是证明可信，不追求大规模性能\n- **subgraph 同构和精确 small CP 是强项**；scheduling、大规模 routing 没有公开的强 benchmark\n- 跟 CP-SAT 比，**性能差 1-2 个数量级**是预期的——证明开销本来就大，且为可验证性保留了简单编码\n\n## 8. Python 集成路径\n\n| 路径 | Pumpkin | Glasgow |\n|---|---|---|\n| 直接 pip | `pip install pumpkin-solver` ✅ | `pip install gcspy`（极早期）⚠️ |\n| CPMpy 后端 | `cp.SolverLookup.get(\"pumpkin\")` ✅ | `cp.SolverLookup.get(\"gcs\")` ✅ |\n| FlatZinc subprocess | ✅ MiniZinc 后端 | ✅ 自带 minizinc/ 目录 |\n| OR-Tools 互操作 | 无 | 无 |\n\n**对我们项目**：MiniZinc/FlatZinc 路径最稳——把 binding 或 flow 子问题先用 MiniZinc 写一份，subprocess 调两个 solver，完全不用碰 Rust/C++ 编译。CPMpy 路径可以共享 Python 模型代码，但需要把现有 OR-Tools `cp_model.CpModel` 重写一遍。\n\n## 9. 跟 Benders 子问题契合度\n\n| 子问题 | Pumpkin 替换 | Glasgow 替换 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **routing**（70×70 网格路径） | 工程量大：需自拼曼哈顿连通性约束；no_overlap_2d 缺失致命 | 不推荐：规模超出其可验证舒适区 |\n| **binding**（端口分配） | 契合度高：all_different + linear，估计 1-2 周 PoC | 契合度高，且可出 PB 证明（用于审计 binding 步骤）|\n| **flow**（多商品诊断） | 契合度低：缺 flow propagator，等价于纯 LP | 契合度低 |\n| **master placement** | 不推荐：CP-SAT 的搜索/线性弱化领先太多 | 不推荐 |\n\n**最值得 PoC 的切入点**：用 Glasgow 给 binding 子问题出**伪布尔证明**，作为 D 方案\"可证明 UNSAT\"路径的**审计 sidecar**——不是替代，而是给已有 CP-SAT 结果加一层 PB 可验证证书。\n\n## 10. 学习曲线 / 风险\n\n| 维度 | Pumpkin | Glasgow | Chuffed | OR-Tools |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 文档质量 | 中（rustdoc 全 + tutorial 简） | 弱（README + 论文） | 中 | 强 |\n| 社区 | 小（学术圈） | 极小（McCreesh 团队） | 小 | 大 |\n| API 稳定性 | 0.x，会变 | 论文驱动，会变 | 稳定 | 工业级稳定 |\n| Python 一手 | pip 可用 | pybind11 极早期 | 通过 MiniZinc | 一手原生 |\n| 大规模性能 | 中（Bronze MiniZinc 2025） | 弱 | 中 | 强 |\n| UNSAT 证书 | DRAT-like | OPB+PBP / VeriPB | 无 | 无（assumptions core 只是子集） |\n| 7 年成熟度对比 | 1 年 | 4 年学术 | 10+ 年 | 7+ 年工业 |\n\n## 11. 2026 最新进展\n\n- **Pumpkin 0.3.0 之后**（2026-02 起）：截至搜索时点没有新 release，commits 仍在 main 推进，重点在 fzn-rs parser 拆分和 proof checker 集成\n- **Glasgow**：AAAI 2026《Faster Certified Symmetry Breaking using Orders with Auxiliary Variables》（McCreesh + Bogaerts + Nordström 等共 11 人）刚发，方向是对称破缺证明加速——跟我们 70×70 grid 对称性其实强相关\n- **其他新 LCG**：PicatSAT 仍在 MiniZinc 2025 Free/Parallel 拿银，但它是 SAT 编码而非真 LCG；没有发现 SolverHub 这类新条目\n\n---\n\n## 关键链接\n\n- [ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin](https://github.com/ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin)\n- [pumpkin-solver crate](https://docs.rs/pumpkin-solver/latest/pumpkin_solver/)\n- [ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver](https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver)\n- [mmcilree/gcspy (Python)](https://github.com/mmcilree/gcspy)\n- [CPMpy Pumpkin interface](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/solvers/pumpkin.html)\n- [MiniZinc Challenge 2025 Results](https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2025/results/)\n- [Ciaran McCreesh papers](https://ciaranm.github.io/)\n\n## 对项目的具体集成评估\n\n**结论：暂不值得作为主求解器替代，但 Glasgow 值得作为 Phase 4 审计 sidecar 做 1 周 PoC。**\n\n具体建议：\n\n1. **Pumpkin 不替换 master/routing**——CP-SAT 在 70×70 placement 上的 7 年工业沉淀不是 0.3.0 阶段的 Pumpkin 能撼动的（MiniZinc Bronze 已说明问题）\n2. **Pumpkin 可以小范围试 binding 子问题**：CPMpy `pumpkin` backend，1-2 周写一个 shadow 验证，对比 OR-Tools 同问题求解时间。**仅当 binding 是当前性能瓶颈时才值得**\n3. **Glasgow 做 D 方案的\"PB 可验证证书\"sidecar**：把 binding 或 routing 子问题（小规模）转 OPB → 喂 Glasgow → 出 PBP → VeriPB 验证。这不是替代 CP-SAT，是**给关键步骤加形式化证明**，符合我们 Phase 3B \"可信精确\"的方向。工程量预估 1-2 周（MiniZinc 路径）\n4. **不推荐**：把任一者当 master 主求解器；当前主要风险是 Glasgow 的 Python 接口（gcspy 7 commits、0 stars）成熟度不够，subprocess + FlatZinc 是更稳的路径\n5. **AI 安全合约影响**：两个 solver 都不写 `data/checkpoints/`，纯辅助验证，不违反 AI Safety Contract——但要注意 Glasgow 的 PB 证书**不能**作为我们 `certified_exact` 的主证明源，只能作为审计层\n\n最后，本机磁盘检查在调研任务里不涉及（纯网络 IO，零写盘）。"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":177,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1567,"cache_read_input_tokens":39404,"output_tokens":4764,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1567},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":177,"output_tokens":4764,"cache_read_input_tokens":39404,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1567,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotjQ2tjBDPpf6VF1xok","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a1aed3c-21c6-4da0-a54b-b94f02a2943d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:11.335Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
